## Introduction

Integrating a point of sale (POS) terminal with Centrapay APIs allows merchants to accept payment via any Centrapay-enabled apps without installing additional POS hardware or software.

## Payment Flow

- [QR Code Flow](/guides/merchant-integration-qr-code-flow): the POS displays a QR code for the patron to scan with their Centrapay app.
- [Barcode Flow](/guides/merchant-integration-barcode-flow): the POS scans a barcode presented by the patron.

## Interface Guidelines

Please use the [Centrapay Brand Assets](https://centrapay.com/brand-assets/) when building the UI for Centrapay payments.

- **Payment option:** Show Centrapay as a payment option the cashier can clearly see. If Farmlands is the only payment option the merchant accepts, show **Farmlands** instead.
- **QR codes:** Display Centrapay QR codes with the Centrapay logo in the centre.
- **Payment status:** Clearly show the current status of the [Payment Request](/api/payment-requests#payment-request-model), and update it as soon as the status changes.
- **Payment method:** Show the payment method used on the customer-facing interface or receipt, using the description in the Payment Request's [`paidBy`](/api/payment-requests#paid-by-model) field.
- **Receipts:** Print the Payment Request `id` or `shortCode` on the receipt so it can be used for [refunds](/guides/initiating-refunds).
